  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Organisations and communities pay for careful work, reliable records and good communication. They judge you by honesty, safety and consistency.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is keeping a clear, dated field note that someone else can use.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and careers for people who love animals and wildlife: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools help identify species from photos, summarise papers and draft reports. Routine record handling shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Fieldcraft, ethics and trust hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to learn and organise notes; later, own your fieldwork and decisions.
  </p>

